WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.440
Hello everyone, welcome back to the Stages of the Path.

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:12.580
Today we're going to review the entire course.

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:16.580
This is good for me, and I wanted to review it myself.

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:24.280
This method of teaching by dividing the video into episodes at different times

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:27.560
easily loses the continuity of the entire course.

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:32.720
I think we can start from the beginning today and

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:38.160
review the teachings we covered in this stage of the Stages of the Path.

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:41.600
I plan to review using the "reading images" approach, the same way

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:47.540
we teach ACI teachers.

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:51.560
We require ACI teachers to be able to

00:00:51.560 --> 00:00:56.360
look at a picture and then say what they taught.

00:00:56.360 --> 00:01:00.140
Tim, how many pictures have we covered? Probably over a thousand, right?

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:02.800
How many? There are

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:05.400
about 500 pictures.

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:12.320
Using pictures for exams makes it easy to assess someone.

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:14.460
We just need to show these pictures.

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:18.120
So, I'll challenge everyone.

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:20.240
When I show you a picture,

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:23.360
I'll give you a little time

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:27.100
to see if you remember what it's about.

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:31.820
This is a good way to review the entire course we've taught.

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:33.680
Okay, let's begin.

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:38.540
Please show the first picture, Mr. Sergi.

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:42.740
This picture is a reminder that

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:50.080
we're talking about the stages of practice for intermediate-level practitioners (the middle path).

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:53.860
They are trying to attain Nirvana.

00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:59.360
They are trying to free themselves from the cycle of life and all personal suffering.

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:03.400
The Buddha taught three trainings here (the three trainings),

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:07.120
three trainings to help you attain personal Nirvana. The

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:12.420
third training is understanding emptiness, understanding the "story of the pen" (wisdom). The

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:15.880
second training is meditation (concentration).

00:02:16.060 --> 00:02:17.660
On a deeper level,

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:21.200
these two trainings can only be done in a very quiet place,

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:27.260
at a specific time of day, when you are truly focused sitting on your meditation mat. On a

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:30.540
deeper level,

00:02:30.700 --> 00:02:34.380
these two trainings should be done at a special time of day.

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:39.360
And this one is also the foundation of the above two trainings, namely, treating others kindly. It

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:41.880
can also be called "morality."

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:44.480
You can call it a moral way of life (morality),

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:48.800
but ultimately it's about treating others kindly.

00:02:48.920 --> 00:02:51.400
This is the foundation.

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:54.280
We can do this training all day long.

00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:58.500
It's one of the three extraordinary trainings (the three trainings) in Buddhism,

00:02:58.520 --> 00:03:01.460
meaning it can help us attain Nirvana.

00:03:01.460 --> 00:03:04.300
We can practice it all day long.

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:05.880
So in this picture,

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:10.360
you can see Sergi teaching Geshe Michael how to use a computer.

00:03:10.520 --> 00:03:15.180
This is one of the best things young people can do for older people.

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:18.480
Next picture,

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:22.100
see if you remember what this picture is about. Can you

00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:27.520
guess?

00:03:27.520 --> 00:03:29.680
This woman is filling out her tax form.

00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:34.260
This is discussed throughout this session of the Stages of the Path teachings. How will this affect her?

00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:37.780
This will make her... a Dharma Master.

00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:41.880
When I say Dharma Master or Tantric Master,

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:44.540
I know you'll picture

00:03:44.540 --> 00:03:49.140
a great lama sitting on a throne, wearing a large yellow hat.

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:57.760
Maybe they're shaking a vajra bell or striking a small drum (chanting scriptures).

00:03:57.760 --> 00:03:59.660
You're thinking: Oh, that's a Dharma Master.

00:03:59.740 --> 00:04:00.860
That's a true Dharma Master.

00:04:00.860 --> 00:04:04.580
Or you might think of Nagarjuna in an old photograph,

00:04:04.580 --> 00:04:06.740
looking very mysterious.

00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:12.120
But actually, in the Stages of the Path, we learn that,

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:14.980
like this lady,

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:17.960
she's married, has several children,

00:04:18.240 --> 00:04:22.580
and she's a Dharma Master, a true Dharma Master.

00:04:22.640 --> 00:04:24.260
Pabongka Rinpoche said:

00:04:24.260 --> 00:04:28.840
Don't think that a Dharma Master necessarily sits on a high throne

00:04:28.840 --> 00:04:30.920
reciting some Tantric rituals.

00:04:30.920 --> 00:04:33.960
What is this lady doing?

00:04:34.940 --> 00:04:38.060
She was paying taxes.

00:04:38.560 --> 00:04:43.520
In my country, paying taxes honestly is really difficult. It can take

00:04:43.880 --> 00:04:46.880
weeks. Paying taxes

00:04:47.140 --> 00:04:49.140
carefully and

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:51.320
completely honestly,

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:54.160
paying every penny you owe—

00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:56.400
these things made her…

00:04:56.480 --> 00:05:01.120
She underwent the first extraordinary training (precept) of a good person: treating

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:02.880
others kindly.

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:05.400
This made her a true master of Buddhism.

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:10.800
Forget about those pictures of lamas wearing big hats and shaking bells and vajras.

00:05:11.020 --> 00:05:13.420
That's easy; everyone can do that.

00:05:14.520 --> 00:05:17.180
But treating others kindly is difficult.

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:21.860
Adhering to morality and codes of conduct is also difficult.

00:05:22.060 --> 00:05:24.700
Next picture.

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:31.860
I'll give you some time. Do you remember what this picture is about?

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:36.220
The quote from the Stages of the Path is:

00:05:36.280 --> 00:05:39.240
TSUL KHRIMS LDAN PA'I DGE SLONG 'OD DANG LDAN.

00:05:39.540 --> 00:05:42.940
A person who truly upholds the precepts, who

00:05:42.940 --> 00:05:47.740
truly follows the Buddhist guidelines, especially the ten guidelines,

00:05:47.740 --> 00:05:50.460
will shine brightly, truly radiantly.

00:05:50.460 --> 00:05:59.180
A person who healthily, humbly, and modestly strives to keep their promises,

00:05:59.180 --> 00:06:02.160
upholds the ten virtuous deeds, and treats

00:06:02.160 --> 00:06:04.000
others kindly,

00:06:04.240 --> 00:06:08.040
will have a certain peaceful expression on their face.

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:10.160
They are radiating light.

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:12.260
When they enter the room,

00:06:12.260 --> 00:06:14.800
everyone begins to feel better,

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:17.760
like Tim and Serge.

00:06:18.740 --> 00:06:20.080
That is the light of the world.

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:24.260
The Buddha said: Those people are the light of the world.

00:06:24.860 --> 00:06:26.720
There is a saying in Christianity:

00:06:26.720 --> 00:06:29.300
Don't put your candle under the basket.

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:33.920
Let the world see your smiling face.

00:06:33.940 --> 00:06:40.820
This is the true guiding light of the whole world.

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:44.620
Next, picture 4.

00:06:48.580 --> 00:06:51.360
This is the cliff. My

00:06:51.360 --> 00:06:56.560
partner Veronica and I went there to celebrate her birthday.

00:06:56.560 --> 00:06:59.460
During this Stages of the Path teaching,

00:07:00.100 --> 00:07:07.340
they were discussing sunset. The Tibetan word is NUB PA, which

00:07:07.460 --> 00:07:09.100
also means "west"

00:07:09.100 --> 00:07:10.900
because the sun sets in the west.

00:07:10.900 --> 00:07:13.360
NUB PA means sunset.

00:07:14.180 --> 00:07:17.060
This verb is sad.

00:07:17.060 --> 00:07:21.400
In Buddhism, this is also a very sad concept.

00:07:21.400 --> 00:07:25.020
Its most famous source is at the end of the Abhidharmakośa,

00:07:25.020 --> 00:07:27.580
also known as the Treasury of Higher Wisdom,

00:07:27.980 --> 00:07:32.500
Vasubandhu's *Treasury of Higher Knowledge*, where he says:

00:07:32.960 --> 00:07:39.060
"The sun of the Dharma, the light of the Dharma, will set in this world."

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:41.600
Our world will lose the light of the Dharma.

00:07:41.600 --> 00:07:43.760
This world will go into darkness.

00:07:43.880 --> 00:07:45.960
After a certain period, the

00:07:46.080 --> 00:07:49.720
Buddha's teachings will disappear from this world.

00:07:49.940 --> 00:07:52.940
They will first disappear from human consciousness,

00:07:52.940 --> 00:07:55.920
but will still exist in libraries.

00:07:56.060 --> 00:07:57.640
These books will still be in libraries,

00:07:57.680 --> 00:08:00.220
perhaps in libraries that John Brady hasn't discovered yet. After

00:08:00.320 --> 00:08:03.520
that, they will also disappear from libraries

00:08:03.520 --> 00:08:05.960
and cease to exist.

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:08.600
I put this image here

00:08:08.600 --> 00:08:11.840
because Pabongka Rinpoche raised a special point.

00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:15.700
He said: If you cannot keep your promises,

00:08:15.780 --> 00:08:20.040
if you cannot treat others with kindness,

00:08:20.040 --> 00:08:23.120
then we can say that the Dharma has left this world. The

00:08:23.120 --> 00:08:27.120
light of the Dharma has left your inner world. In

00:08:27.120 --> 00:08:31.080
your own heart, the sun has set.

00:08:31.080 --> 00:08:32.620
This is really sad

00:08:32.620 --> 00:08:34.880
if we cannot uphold the precepts (that will happen).

00:08:34.960 --> 00:08:36.640
Next image:

00:08:43.560 --> 00:08:48.860
Our retreat is called "Love in the Time of Pandemic."

00:08:49.520 --> 00:08:55.520
The focus is: When the world is going through very difficult times,

00:08:55.600 --> 00:08:57.940
if you can keep your promises,

00:08:57.940 --> 00:09:00.860
if you treat others with kindness,

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:04.320
when things are causing panic and fear, when the virus is spreading...

00:09:04.320 --> 00:09:06.740
We don't know which direction things will take, or how they will develop. We

00:09:06.800 --> 00:09:09.820
don't know how many people will die.

00:09:10.200 --> 00:09:16.860
If you do something kind to others during such a difficult time, the

00:09:16.880 --> 00:09:19.160
seeds will be even stronger.

00:09:19.360 --> 00:09:23.280
He mentioned that if you remember the five-star Buddha Paradise, it's like

00:09:23.280 --> 00:09:26.180
an exceptionally perfect place. It's

00:09:26.400 --> 00:09:28.260
easy to be a good person there.

00:09:28.260 --> 00:09:30.780
Everyone there is a good person. It's

00:09:30.780 --> 00:09:33.540
not a great achievement, not a big deal.

00:09:33.600 --> 00:09:38.440
And the seeds planted by being kind among a group of good people aren't
that strong.

00:09:38.880 --> 00:09:43.660
When people attack you, when people are worried, be kind.

00:09:43.840 --> 00:09:46.720
When everyone is not treating each other kindly,

00:09:46.940 --> 00:09:54.060
be the one who stands up and shares things in difficult times.

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:57.340
That kind of person is extremely pure.

00:09:57.520 --> 00:10:01.500
That's immense karma, incredible karma, even more powerful.

00:10:01.500 --> 00:10:04.380
I think this pandemic is a very good opportunity.

00:10:04.560 --> 00:10:07.680
For all of us, it's a great opportunity to show whether

00:10:07.840 --> 00:10:10.680
we are true Buddhist disciples. Are

00:10:11.160 --> 00:10:14.220
we truly practicing the Bodhisattva path? Even when things are going

00:10:15.060 --> 00:10:18.560
badly, will we still help others? The

00:10:19.580 --> 00:10:21.580
next

00:10:28.480 --> 00:10:31.780
image is hard to remember; I can hardly recall it myself.

00:10:31.780 --> 00:10:37.600
I'll give you some time to try and remember it.

00:10:40.760 --> 00:10:45.040
Pabongka Rinpoche quoted some books, and

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:49.240
in the endings of different books,

00:10:49.240 --> 00:10:51.600
he quoted a famous prayer:

00:10:51.600 --> 00:10:54.840
BLO BZANG RGYAL BA'I BSTAN PA ... CIG BLO BZANG RGYAL BA'I BSTAN PA ... CIG.

00:10:54.840 --> 00:10:56.720
This

00:10:56.720 --> 00:10:58.120
means, "

00:10:58.120 --> 00:11:07.940
May the teachings of His Holiness Lobsang Tsongkhapa spread throughout the world (especially His Holiness the Venerable One,
may the essence of the Holy Teachings shine eternally)." You might think: We should go online and translate the Stages of the Path into

00:11:08.840 --> 00:11:10.780


00:11:10.780 --> 00:11:16.780
multiple languages.

00:11:17.280 --> 00:11:22.300
We should strive to spread these good words to as many people as possible. This is the last

00:11:22.560 --> 00:11:25.000
sentence of the prayer, which

00:11:25.000 --> 00:11:31.420
also means that after we leave the classroom where the Stages of the Path are taught or after watching the recording, we

00:11:31.420 --> 00:11:35.860
should share the Dharma with others.

00:11:35.860 --> 00:11:38.400
We should spread the Dharma throughout the world.

00:11:38.400 --> 00:11:44.260
In this section on the Stages of the Path, Pabongka Rinpoche said: "

00:11:44.320 --> 00:11:50.660
The place where you spread the Dharma should be here, in your own heart.

00:11:50.900 --> 00:11:53.760
Don't think that spreading the Dharma is just about

00:11:53.760 --> 00:11:58.720
trying to translate videos into more languages.

00:11:58.720 --> 00:12:01.280
That's a very important way to spread the Dharma."

00:12:01.440 --> 00:12:05.660
But he said: If you spread it in your own heart,

00:12:05.920 --> 00:12:08.360
then the Dharma will definitely spread outwards

00:12:08.360 --> 00:12:10.140
because the world comes from your heart,

00:12:10.140 --> 00:12:12.160
in fact, from your heart chakra.

00:12:12.320 --> 00:12:16.860
Next, picture 7.

00:12:19.280 --> 00:12:21.720
Try to recall what this picture is. I

00:12:21.820 --> 00:12:25.380
will give you some time.

00:12:28.680 --> 00:12:31.880
I really like this theme:

00:12:32.400 --> 00:12:42.160
having an intimate relationship with another person, like these two people. In my

00:12:43.660 --> 00:12:45.940
opinion, in Vajrayana,

00:12:45.940 --> 00:12:48.100
this is one of the happiest things that happen to you.

00:12:48.100 --> 00:12:52.400
This is one of the best things that happen to you.

00:12:52.800 --> 00:12:54.640
Anyone can tell you that the

00:12:54.640 --> 00:13:00.120
whole world is looking for a partner because it makes people happy. When things are going well,

00:13:00.120 --> 00:13:04.120
it is one of the greatest happinesses. This is one of the greatest

00:13:04.720 --> 00:13:08.360
happinesses you can have.

00:13:08.360 --> 00:13:13.340
But you and I both know that when things aren't going well,

00:13:13.520 --> 00:13:16.720
this is the greatest misfortune in life.

00:13:16.960 --> 00:13:21.320
Why is this relevant to this lesson?

00:13:24.000 --> 00:13:29.540
If you uphold morality (observance), this is the happiest thing in your

00:13:29.540 --> 00:13:31.920
life.

00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:36.880
But if you break the precepts, the same thing will cause you great pain. Just like having a wonderful woman or

00:13:36.980 --> 00:13:41.020
man as your partner—someone who brings you immense

00:13:41.280 --> 00:13:44.620
joy can also cause you unbearable suffering. So in this case, the precepts

00:13:44.660 --> 00:13:47.720


00:13:47.720 --> 00:13:49.600


00:13:49.600 --> 00:13:56.240
—the personal practice of kindness and good deeds—are likened to a partner. He/she can create the best or the worst

00:13:56.240 --> 00:14:00.300
thing in your life

00:14:00.320 --> 00:14:03.880
—the same person. Next, picture 8. This picture is difficult to understand; see if you remember it.

00:14:04.060 --> 00:14:08.440


00:14:11.660 --> 00:14:15.060


00:14:15.520 --> 00:14:18.100
I'll take a small sip of green juice first. Thank you, Vimala. Actually, this represents breaking a promise.

00:14:18.720 --> 00:14:20.720


00:14:29.700 --> 00:14:33.820


00:14:34.060 --> 00:14:39.720
Pulling out this weed represents breaking a promise. Why is destroying this plant breaking a promise? If you are a gardener,

00:14:39.760 --> 00:14:45.260


00:14:45.440 --> 00:14:47.140


00:14:47.340 --> 00:14:55.020
you know you should pull weeds before the seeds sprout. If you wait until the seeds are almost falling off before pulling up a plant,

00:14:55.420 --> 00:14:59.520


00:14:59.680 --> 00:15:02.180


00:15:02.180 --> 00:15:05.440
you will have sown thousands more seeds. The following month, the following year, thousands upon thousands of weeds will grow.

00:15:05.680 --> 00:15:11.260


00:15:11.260 --> 00:15:14.360
So you must remove these weeds early. This refers to a very extreme statement made by the Buddha: DGE SLONG DAG SROG DANG

00:15:14.720 --> 00:15:22.100


00:15:22.100 --> 00:15:26.180
 
BRAL ZHING SHI BA NI BLA'I It is better to die than to break a vow. Why? When you break a vow,

00:15:28.500 --> 00:15:32.060


00:15:32.280 --> 00:15:33.500


00:15:33.680 --> 00:15:35.680


00:15:35.760 --> 00:15:38.980
you are activating seeds that will continue to sow seeds for many lifetimes. If you die, you destroy a complex of body and consciousness. If

00:15:39.120 --> 00:15:43.100


00:15:43.280 --> 00:15:49.740
you die, you destroy a very useful temple—a tangible temple and consciousness; you lose a complex. But if you break a promise (break a vow), you lose many complexes of body and consciousness. You destroy bodies

00:15:50.480 --> 00:15:54.380


00:15:54.380 --> 00:15:58.340
and consciousness for many lifetimes. You are like setting seeds in motion; they will destroy lives for many lifetimes. The Buddha said: "I would rather die than

00:15:58.560 --> 00:16:01.080
break a vow." When he said he would rather die than break a vow, he wasn't using a metaphor;

00:16:01.280 --> 00:16:05.000


00:16:05.000 --> 00:16:07.960


00:16:08.720 --> 00:16:11.440


00:16:11.440 --> 00:16:14.280


00:16:14.340 --> 00:16:20.020


00:16:20.160 --> 00:16:31.720
 
he was speaking the truth. There's a joke in the Stages of the Path: We vow never to give up Bodhicitta, even at the cost of our lives. There

00:16:33.540 --> 00:16:36.560
's a famous saying: We spend our whole lives waiting to be

00:16:38.060 --> 00:16:41.680


00:16:41.760 --> 00:16:44.840


00:16:46.720 --> 00:16:52.480


00:16:52.720 --> 00:16:57.160
imprisoned by some evil person who holds a knife and says: "Either give up your Bodhisattva vows, or you die

00:16:57.400 --> 00:17:03.240
today." Then

00:17:03.240 --> 00:17:04.799
we say: "

00:17:04.799 --> 00:17:06.480
I choose to die," and then they kill us. I think all of us have been

00:17:06.480 --> 00:17:10.120


00:17:10.120 --> 00:17:13.920
waiting for this moment since we received our vows. We've been waiting for such a person to threaten us with a

00:17:14.320 --> 00:17:18.300
knife.

00:17:18.300 --> 00:17:20.900
But in reality, we are the ones holding the knife. We

00:17:20.900 --> 00:17:24.260
threaten our Bodhisattva vows every day. We have to

00:17:24.700 --> 00:17:28.500
make this decision every day:

00:17:28.500 --> 00:17:32.700
whether to carefully uphold our vows. It's

00:17:35.340 --> 00:17:38.100
hard to find someone like that—they lock you up in jail and say, "

00:17:38.100 --> 00:17:41.440
If you don't renounce your Bodhisattva vows, I'll kill you." Next picture.

00:17:44.720 --> 00:17:46.720


00:17:48.080 --> 00:17:50.120
See if you remember.

00:17:50.120 --> 00:17:55.240
I'll give you some time to try and recall.

00:18:03.840 --> 00:18:05.840
This represents… We have a mixed-nut

00:18:06.000 --> 00:18:09.039
translation team.

00:18:09.840 --> 00:18:13.440
We were previously translating an ancient Vinaya text, the

00:18:13.840 --> 00:18:16.600
Sangha Vinaya, the Sangha and Nun

00:18:17.120 --> 00:18:19.600
Vinaya. The text mentions this precept:

00:18:19.600 --> 00:18:25.160
There is a tradition that we should not…

00:18:25.340 --> 00:18:27.800
When you ordain as a monk or nun, you receive a robe

00:18:27.820 --> 00:18:32.260
, a small Buddha statue,

00:18:32.940 --> 00:18:35.540
and a filter.

00:18:35.920 --> 00:18:39.920
In ancient India, you were supposed to carry this filter with you. If

00:18:40.080 --> 00:18:43.360
you drink water from a stream, you

00:18:44.000 --> 00:18:46.580
should filter the water first

00:18:46.960 --> 00:18:49.940
to ensure you don't kill any small insects.

00:18:50.400 --> 00:18:55.680
We mentioned a famous tradition in the Vinaya:

00:18:56.240 --> 00:18:59.200
if several monks are going to find water and

00:18:59.420 --> 00:19:02.380
go to a stream to fetch water,

00:19:02.640 --> 00:19:07.880
they should choose the best monk to check the water.

00:19:09.280 --> 00:19:12.620
Don't choose the one who doesn't care about small insects.

00:19:13.400 --> 00:19:15.600
Try to find the one who loves small insects and

00:19:15.840 --> 00:19:19.280
have them check the water, because they will be more careful.

00:19:20.580 --> 00:19:22.000
What's the key point?

00:19:22.640 --> 00:19:26.440
We seem to have discussed some ecological precepts.

00:19:27.040 --> 00:19:32.560
Monks and nuns shouldn't even break the green leaves of plants

00:19:32.560 --> 00:19:37.560
because that's the home of small creatures. This means

00:19:38.060 --> 00:19:43.000
observing even the smallest precepts

00:19:43.000 --> 00:19:44.820
very strictly,

00:19:44.820 --> 00:19:49.680
because the results multiply exponentially.

00:19:49.920 --> 00:19:56.580
Therefore, it's important to observe morality at a very subtle, very nuanced level.

00:19:56.640 --> 00:20:00.000
But don't be nitpicky.

00:20:00.840 --> 00:20:02.820
If I were to

00:20:02.820 --> 00:20:04.720
write about the Bodhisattva precepts, I would add an extra one:

00:20:05.040 --> 00:20:07.420
Don't constantly talk about your Bodhisattva precepts.

00:20:08.200 --> 00:20:11.340
Nothing is more annoying

00:20:11.340 --> 00:20:18.580
than someone telling you they're observing them, so it has to be so bothersome.

00:20:19.760 --> 00:20:24.140
So, observe the precepts happily, joyfully, but not excessively.

00:20:24.140 --> 00:20:26.460
Don't bother others with your precepts because

00:20:26.460 --> 00:20:29.380
precepts aren't meant to bother others. Observe the small precepts quietly. Observe them

00:20:30.560 --> 00:20:32.740


00:20:32.740 --> 00:20:36.120
yourself, don't announce them widely.

00:20:36.320 --> 00:20:38.200
There's an Islamic saying: "The left hand should not let the

00:20:38.200 --> 00:20:42.680
right hand know what it's doing." This means:

00:20:43.040 --> 00:20:47.160
Don't publicize your precepts everywhere, just observe them quietly.

00:20:47.440 --> 00:20:50.300
Observe the precepts at a subtle level.

00:20:50.560 --> 00:20:52.560
Next picture.

00:20:59.200 --> 00:21:09.100
This concept is: Treat others kindly like planting a tree. Today

00:21:09.440 --> 00:21:14.660
I went to the Peach Tree Cafe to check some things. When

00:21:16.000 --> 00:21:21.160
Chen Tang, Xiaoping, and I first started the "Peach Tree Morning Show,"

00:21:21.160 --> 00:21:24.600
we planted a peach tree there.

00:21:24.600 --> 00:21:29.000
I want to tell everyone that three peaches have grown on the tree this week.

00:21:29.120 --> 00:21:32.760
We have peaches now. This

00:21:33.600 --> 00:21:38.820
means that if you take good care of your basic practice, take good care of the foundation, and cultivate

00:21:38.820 --> 00:21:40.420


00:21:40.420 --> 00:21:46.440
good karma through keeping precepts and treating others kindly,

00:21:46.840 --> 00:21:48.860
it will grow into a tree.

00:21:49.040 --> 00:21:53.240
That peach tree was planted about five months ago and

00:21:53.760 --> 00:21:56.560
has already begun to provide a lot of fruit.

00:21:57.220 --> 00:22:01.560
If you don't take good care of it when it's small, you

00:22:01.560 --> 00:22:03.200
won't get anything.

00:22:03.200 --> 00:22:07.560
If you take good care of your Buddhist practice foundation, which

00:22:07.660 --> 00:22:09.680
is to treat others kindly, then there will be

00:22:10.000 --> 00:22:12.800
thousands upon thousands of fruits.

00:22:12.860 --> 00:22:15.920
They will grow into very large trees...

00:22:15.920 --> 00:22:19.560
They will grow into trees and produce peaches every year. Then

00:22:19.600 --> 00:22:23.180
you will harvest peaches for many years.

00:22:23.940 --> 00:22:28.160
This child carefully protects the buds.

00:22:28.620 --> 00:22:30.840
Guard your morality.

00:22:31.320 --> 00:22:33.440
Next picture. If

00:22:34.960 --> 00:22:37.000
I remember correctly, there

00:22:37.120 --> 00:22:43.760
are four conditions that can lead you to break your vows.

00:22:43.760 --> 00:22:46.140
If you have taken the Bodhisattva vows,

00:22:46.400 --> 00:22:49.440
or the Pratimoksha vows,

00:22:49.680 --> 00:22:53.160
or even the Vajrayana secret vows,

00:22:53.880 --> 00:22:56.100
I think there are four of them.

00:22:56.100 --> 00:22:57.380
Pabongka Rinpoche reviewed...

00:22:57.520 --> 00:22:58.840
No, maybe more than that.

00:22:58.840 --> 00:23:03.420
But anyway, there are indeed some conditions that can help you break your vows. If

00:23:03.620 --> 00:23:07.880
you want to break your vows, here are a few special ways.

00:23:07.880 --> 00:23:09.760
The first one is...

00:23:09.760 --> 00:23:15.040
If you don't know what the precepts are,

00:23:15.380 --> 00:23:16.780
this is a good way to break them.

00:23:16.900 --> 00:23:21.060
If you want to break them, don't learn them.

00:23:21.160 --> 00:23:25.980
One of the things I hate most, and many things about Buddhism that I dislike,

00:23:28.120 --> 00:23:32.360
is when teachers give initiations, lots of initiations,

00:23:32.360 --> 00:23:39.600
but don't explain to the recipients that they've just given precepts.

00:23:39.720 --> 00:23:44.120
When you receive an initiation, you also receive hundreds of precepts,

00:23:44.320 --> 00:23:46.960
and if you don't know these precepts, you'll break them.

00:23:46.960 --> 00:23:54.320
Before an initiation, the teacher has a responsibility to train you on the relevant precepts.

00:23:54.960 --> 00:23:57.300
If they don't say they'll explain,

00:23:57.300 --> 00:24:00.380
I won't receive an initiation from them. The

00:24:00.800 --> 00:24:03.160
best way to break a precept is,

00:24:03.160 --> 00:24:06.020
first, not understanding the precepts.

00:24:06.160 --> 00:24:08.900
Look at the recipe before cooking.

00:24:08.900 --> 00:24:11.840
Veronica always says this when I cook.

00:24:12.640 --> 00:24:14.640
Next picture:

00:24:15.520 --> 00:24:21.980
A lady is saying, "It's no big deal."

00:24:23.480 --> 00:24:26.300
That precept is about

00:24:28.380 --> 00:24:32.640
not breaking green plants without praying. Come on, that's a bit much.

00:24:32.940 --> 00:24:35.880


00:24:35.880 --> 00:24:40.220
That's a bit excessive, not that important. It's

00:24:40.320 --> 00:24:41.520
just a few small insects. They

00:24:41.680 --> 00:24:46.140
might occasionally use that leaf as a roof. It

00:24:47.140 --> 00:24:48.720
's not a big deal. The

00:24:48.900 --> 00:24:54.320
second important way to break a precept is to have this attitude:

00:24:54.320 --> 00:24:58.460
"Oh, that one isn't very important; I'm upholding important precepts."

00:24:58.800 --> 00:25:00.800
Next picture:

00:25:04.880 --> 00:25:06.720
If we had Klesha... It

00:25:06.720 --> 00:25:13.780
means: If you let certain negative emotions run rampant in your mind,

00:25:13.780 --> 00:25:15.600
this is a good way to break your vows. Getting

00:25:15.600 --> 00:25:19.740
annoyed by others,

00:25:19.740 --> 00:25:24.920
or being obsessed with getting something or money, or being

00:25:25.440 --> 00:25:28.320
attracted to Netflix (a movie website) at night. By

00:25:28.720 --> 00:25:33.100
the way, there's nothing wrong with watching Netflix videos. What

00:25:33.300 --> 00:25:40.360
I'm saying is, hurting others because you want to go home and watch Netflix is

00:25:40.360 --> 00:25:41.700
a problem.

00:25:43.360 --> 00:25:45.440
This is called "gang fight".

00:25:45.440 --> 00:25:47.640
What's the story?

00:25:51.080 --> 00:25:55.000
Head straight for the biggest leader of the other group.

00:25:55.520 --> 00:25:57.960
Find out who the leader is.

00:25:58.160 --> 00:26:02.660
Don't speak, don't negotiate, don't shout at each other.

00:26:02.740 --> 00:26:05.980
Just walk up to him and strike him on the head.

00:26:06.080 --> 00:26:09.340
Then the entire gang will collapse.

00:26:09.580 --> 00:26:13.660
Identify your worst bad habit and

00:26:13.760 --> 00:26:19.500
pursue it first; this is the method of discipline.

00:26:19.700 --> 00:26:21.700
Next picture.

00:26:25.400 --> 00:26:29.700
By the way, at my age—

00:26:29.700 --> 00:26:32.320
I'm not trying to tell you how old I am—

00:26:32.320 --> 00:26:35.760
all the things that young people love

00:26:35.760 --> 00:26:40.320
seem ridiculous to someone my age.

00:26:40.960 --> 00:26:44.520
I have some experience with

00:26:44.960 --> 00:26:46.880
things like:

00:26:46.880 --> 00:26:49.880
Oh, she's the most beautiful woman in the world.

00:26:50.000 --> 00:26:52.860
He's the most handsome man in the world.

00:26:53.040 --> 00:26:59.860
First of all, my brother once said something very funny:

00:26:59.980 --> 00:27:00.860
He said, "Do you like that girl?"

00:27:00.920 --> 00:27:01.960
I said: Yes. He

00:27:02.080 --> 00:27:03.940
said: Do you want to spend your life with her?

00:27:03.940 --> 00:27:04.480
I said: Yes.

00:27:04.640 --> 00:27:07.540
He said: Let's find out about her mother first,

00:27:07.680 --> 00:27:09.900
see what her mother looks like.

00:27:09.900 --> 00:27:12.760
I said: Her mother is very ugly, overweight.

00:27:12.760 --> 00:27:15.440
She looks very tired and scary.

00:27:15.440 --> 00:27:20.400
Then he said: What do you think her mother looked like when she was young?

00:27:20.400 --> 00:27:22.160
So think about it.

00:27:24.080 --> 00:27:28.520
If you're fixated on someone's appearance,

00:27:29.000 --> 00:27:31.280
or external conditions,

00:27:31.280 --> 00:27:34.020
or things that aren't important to them,

00:27:34.100 --> 00:27:37.260
those things change. You'll see them get sick, see

00:27:37.300 --> 00:27:42.680
them age, see them have diarrhea and vomit.

00:27:42.880 --> 00:27:44.380
If you're not so lucky,

00:27:44.400 --> 00:27:47.440
you might even sometimes see their internal organs during surgery.

00:27:47.600 --> 00:27:50.800
Don't deceive yourself:

00:27:51.240 --> 00:27:57.540
thinking it's worth hurting someone to get the most beautiful woman or man.

00:27:57.700 --> 00:27:59.780
It's not worth it. It

00:28:00.740 --> 00:28:02.780
won't last.

00:28:04.420 --> 00:28:07.820
Having a relationship is good, but get it for a good reason. Next.

00:28:07.840 --> 00:28:09.840


00:28:11.520 --> 00:28:14.420
If you have a problem with getting angry

00:28:14.640 --> 00:28:16.640
or easily angered,

00:28:16.960 --> 00:28:22.500
then imagine giving this person something they want.

00:28:22.680 --> 00:28:24.480
This is called maitre-

00:28:24.800 --> 00:28:26.080
jampa-

00:28:26.080 --> 00:28:26.800
love.

00:28:26.800 --> 00:28:29.620
Visualize, try to imagine

00:28:29.720 --> 00:28:34.700
how wonderful it would be to give them what they love and want.

00:28:34.820 --> 00:28:36.480
Try to cultivate this attitude.

00:28:36.480 --> 00:28:41.320
If you're unfriendly to another person,

00:28:41.520 --> 00:28:45.260
then fantasize, that is, meditate,

00:28:45.520 --> 00:28:49.520
imagine giving them something they really like.

00:28:49.680 --> 00:28:51.680
Next.

00:28:52.720 --> 00:28:56.300
I'll give you some time.

00:28:56.300 --> 00:28:59.700
I bet you can't remember what this picture is.

00:29:00.000 --> 00:29:03.620
Tim is cheating (rewind).

00:29:06.100 --> 00:29:08.940
What is this picture?

00:29:09.680 --> 00:29:12.880
This image is about arrogance.

00:29:13.560 --> 00:29:17.400
Arrogance can also be an obstacle to upholding precepts.

00:29:17.400 --> 00:29:23.000
This book talks about the

00:29:23.180 --> 00:29:27.760
most common kind of arrogance in monasteries,

00:29:27.760 --> 00:29:35.800
which is how much you know about the scriptures and how many facts you've collected in your life.

00:29:36.000 --> 00:29:40.180
I really enjoy this: collecting obscure Buddhist facts.

00:29:40.340 --> 00:29:45.660
The more you collect, the more special you feel.

00:29:46.660 --> 00:29:50.300
Pabongka Rinpoche said: All the Buddhist teachings you've studied in your life, all the

00:29:50.300 --> 00:29:51.480
things you've memorized,

00:29:51.480 --> 00:29:53.300
all the things you've debated,

00:29:53.300 --> 00:29:56.080
all the Geshe degrees you've obtained—

00:29:57.100 --> 00:30:00.520
compared to the things you still don't know,

00:30:00.520 --> 00:30:02.000
you know very little.

00:30:02.000 --> 00:30:06.520
You're like a tiny worm in the ocean.

00:30:07.460 --> 00:30:11.200
Sometimes you go out and look up at the stars.

00:30:12.020 --> 00:30:14.740
Many stars have planets orbiting them. There are

00:30:15.120 --> 00:30:19.880
people on those planets, and we need to know a lot about them. What

00:30:20.000 --> 00:30:23.100
we know, what

00:30:23.280 --> 00:30:25.880
we're proud of,

00:30:26.240 --> 00:30:32.420
is only a very, very small part of what we can understand.

00:30:33.820 --> 00:30:35.840
So don't be arrogant. The next image is one of the

00:30:35.840 --> 00:30:37.840


00:30:40.780 --> 00:30:48.560
temptations that cause you to break precepts, break promises, or violate morality. One of the

00:30:48.620 --> 00:30:50.660


00:30:50.680 --> 00:30:57.020
temptations that prevents you from reaching Nirvana, the second level of the path—personal Nirvana,

00:30:57.280 --> 00:31:00.080
is (not) understanding emptiness, (not) studying emptiness.

00:31:00.240 --> 00:31:02.240
If you recognize the

00:31:02.380 --> 00:31:07.600
harsh things others have done to you... If it

00:31:08.080 --> 00:31:11.880
comes directly from what you did last week,

00:31:12.480 --> 00:31:15.180
then you won't make a big mistake. The

00:31:15.560 --> 00:31:21.500
more you learn about emptiness, the more you learn about cause and effect, dependent origination—

00:31:21.680 --> 00:31:24.640
meaning this person comes from my seeds—

00:31:24.980 --> 00:31:31.180
then it will be easier for you to keep the precepts.

00:31:31.180 --> 00:31:33.120
So learn, learn, and learn some more.

00:31:34.180 --> 00:31:40.340
I had a teacher, an elderly teacher from Inner Mongolia,

00:31:41.200 --> 00:31:45.100
very old, suffering from tuberculosis.

00:31:45.340 --> 00:31:47.260
He once said:

00:31:47.280 --> 00:31:53.260
He's good, you're proud, you have a lot to be proud of.

00:31:53.260 --> 00:31:55.260
Graduated from Princeton University,

00:31:55.600 --> 00:31:57.279
then got a Geshe degree.

00:31:57.280 --> 00:31:59.280
These are all very useful, very useful.

00:32:00.320 --> 00:32:02.980
You'll work harder to push yourself, to make

00:32:03.040 --> 00:32:05.040
yourself look smart.

00:32:05.120 --> 00:32:10.200
That's lucky, but later try to give up these things and

00:32:10.500 --> 00:32:12.820
just learn to be a good person. It's

00:32:12.820 --> 00:32:14.760
funny.

00:32:14.760 --> 00:32:18.260
He gave me the Adam (translated) scripture on his deathbed.

00:32:18.320 --> 00:32:20.320
I still remember it. Next

00:32:22.720 --> 00:32:24.640
picture.

00:32:25.520 --> 00:32:28.960
Technically, this is the fourth cause.

00:32:30.320 --> 00:32:35.280
One of the causes that makes you break your vows or break your promises is:

00:32:36.140 --> 00:32:38.800
In modern society, when you're busy, it's

00:32:38.800 --> 00:32:43.280
hard to keep your consciousness on the precepts.

00:32:43.280 --> 00:32:45.520
Things are moving so fast.

00:32:45.520 --> 00:32:48.120
There are thousands of things to see on the internet.

00:32:48.920 --> 00:32:51.680
Life changes so quickly that it's

00:32:51.680 --> 00:32:57.220
hard to maintain this self-awareness: Have

00:32:57.220 --> 00:33:02.380
I broken my vows? Did I do anything to hurt others?

00:33:02.880 --> 00:33:07.260
You need to slow down a bit and return to the precepts. Remain sensitive to the fact that

00:33:07.600 --> 00:33:17.860
you've promised yourself not to hurt others. The busier you are,


00:33:18.740 --> 00:33:22.640
the more careful you need to be.

00:33:23.160 --> 00:33:29.700
When you're busy, it's even easy to get angry with your partner.

00:33:29.700 --> 00:33:32.360
They try to tell you something.

00:33:32.480 --> 00:33:36.640
You're busy handling 10 things at work.

00:33:36.640 --> 00:33:40.280
You might say, "I don't have time to listen to you right now." "My

00:33:40.580 --> 00:33:44.480
boss assigned me 10 things." These are

00:33:45.320 --> 00:33:48.040
precisely the times you should slow down,

00:33:48.040 --> 00:33:49.840
return to the precepts, and

00:33:49.920 --> 00:33:53.520
not forget your promise to be kind to others. Even if you're stressed,

00:33:54.200 --> 00:33:56.940
busy,

00:33:58.740 --> 00:34:01.860
or breaking some business promises, it's better than being tense, anxious, and unfriendly to others, even if it means not paying bills, missing

00:34:01.960 --> 00:34:08.720


00:34:09.040 --> 00:34:13.280
business meetings,

00:34:13.940 --> 00:34:16.460
or not putting in your best effort at

00:34:16.700 --> 00:34:21.600


00:34:23.600 --> 00:34:25.600


00:34:25.920 --> 00:34:30.660
work. If it helps

00:34:32.180 --> 00:34:34.180
you stay clear-headed, then it's even better. Next picture: This woman is buying something useless in a store. See if you can remember this story. She said, "

00:34:35.360 --> 00:34:37.880
Oh, this box is so pretty!"

00:34:37.880 --> 00:34:41.000


00:34:41.200 --> 00:34:43.600


00:34:43.760 --> 00:34:47.500


00:34:47.680 --> 00:34:49.440
She went to a department store and bought this box. What was that home goods store called? Is this a place to buy things? Like Crate and Barrel,

00:34:49.440 --> 00:34:52.820
she went to a Crate and Barrel store in the US and said, "Oh, my husband will love this box." She had no

00:34:53.120 --> 00:34:56.500
idea what the box was

00:34:56.640 --> 00:34:59.280


00:35:03.280 --> 00:35:05.760


00:35:05.760 --> 00:35:08.440
for, but she just wanted to take it home. When she got home, her husband said, "Are you crazy?" This little box is

00:35:08.440 --> 00:35:10.720
completely useless. We already have enough junk at home.

00:35:10.820 --> 00:35:14.120


00:35:15.440 --> 00:35:20.840
Should she return it and get a refund? Should she go back to the gas station and try to return it? No, this

00:35:22.720 --> 00:35:25.440


00:35:25.440 --> 00:35:29.500


00:35:29.860 --> 00:35:32.460
box wasn't bought from there. That's obvious, but we still have to say this: what if you bought a useless box because

00:35:32.720 --> 00:35:35.060
you liked it, and you thought your husband would like it too

00:35:35.060 --> 00:35:37.520


00:35:37.520 --> 00:35:40.140


00:35:40.720 --> 00:35:43.400


00:35:43.400 --> 00:35:45.280


00:35:45.280 --> 00:35:47.280


00:35:54.079 --> 00:35:56.579


00:35:58.240 --> 00:36:01.920


00:36:02.080 --> 00:36:05.280


00:36:05.760 --> 00:36:10.620


00:36:10.860 --> 00:36:14.480


00:36:16.240 --> 00:36:21.260
, but he doesn't? What does it mean if he tells you to return it, but not somewhere else, but back to where you bought it? You have to pay me. When you break the precepts and should repent, try to find the person who gave you the precepts and try to repent in front of that person. Is it okay to repent at home by yourself? Generally speaking, it's not allowed

00:36:21.580 --> 00:36:25.920
if you received the precepts from someone else. If you didn't

00:36:26.020 --> 00:36:30.720


00:36:30.900 --> 00:36:32.880


00:36:33.040 --> 00:36:34.900


00:36:35.120 --> 00:36:38.380
receive the precepts from someone else, you might be able to repent at home in front of a Buddha statue or something similar. In extreme cases, that's

00:36:38.640 --> 00:36:42.360
fine. But generally

00:36:42.360 --> 00:36:44.360


00:36:44.400 --> 00:36:46.600


00:36:46.600 --> 00:36:48.480
speaking, if you can

00:36:48.480 --> 00:36:51.760
find the person who gave you the precepts, open your heart and repent to them, even if it's a bit shameless, okay? Anyway, we're all shameless

00:36:51.840 --> 00:36:54.500


00:36:54.500 --> 00:36:56.000


00:36:56.000 --> 00:37:01.080
these days, so when you're honest

00:37:02.120 --> 00:37:04.660


00:37:04.660 --> 00:37:06.520
about your vows, be a little brazen and say: "Whatever." Go straight to your teacher and say, "I stupidly broke this vow." Then your teacher will say, "Wow, that's terrible."

00:37:06.520 --> 00:37:09.560


00:37:09.700 --> 00:37:11.240
You'll say, "Yeah, yeah," and that's it. You'll feel so clean, so wonderful. You can be a little shy about many things in life, but never be ashamed of breaking your vows (confess). If

00:37:11.240 --> 00:37:12.800


00:37:13.160 --> 00:37:17.000
you've broken a vow, tell someone. And when you do that,

00:37:17.000 --> 00:37:20.300


00:37:20.300 --> 00:37:22.220


00:37:22.220 --> 00:37:25.200
you've cleared the negative seed, and the problem is solved. If you cling to it or keep it a secret, and if you spend more energy hiding it instead of admitting your mistake, that's incredibly

00:37:26.079 --> 00:37:30.319
foolish, and you won't feel good. You won't feel clean. Be honest with your

00:37:32.160 --> 00:37:36.300


00:37:37.220 --> 00:37:40.920
teacher: "I have this problem, I have this bad habit." The karma will be crushed, the seed will be crushed. Your teacher will say, "I've heard that before, you told me before, but you have to keep going

00:37:40.920 --> 00:37:43.700
, keep telling them." Next

00:37:46.960 --> 00:37:48.960


00:37:50.400 --> 00:37:52.960


00:37:59.600 --> 00:38:06.280
picture. This is about… wait, do you remember? Here, once again, it's about respecting the precepts in small details. This is actually about a

00:38:06.280 --> 00:38:12.260
precept for monks: they should brush their teeth

00:38:12.260 --> 00:38:14.940
with a stick called a SO SHING. This is a

00:38:14.940 --> 00:38:17.580
stick

00:38:17.580 --> 00:38:19.920
you use to clean your teeth. You just need to cut it down from a tree, and then

00:38:20.640 --> 00:38:22.640


00:38:22.960 --> 00:38:27.980


00:38:30.400 --> 00:38:32.560


00:38:33.440 --> 00:38:35.519


00:38:35.519 --> 00:38:37.460


00:38:38.160 --> 00:38:40.100


00:38:40.100 --> 00:38:42.880


00:38:42.880 --> 00:38:44.740


00:38:44.900 --> 00:38:47.600
you can use it. It's a toothbrush. What's being said here is: monks should have their own toothbrushes, and you should brush your teeth. This seems like a

00:38:48.540 --> 00:38:52.340
small thing. Wait, I'm trying hard to uphold my Tantric vows, practicing the Dharma to go to Amitabha's Pure Land, and

00:38:52.340 --> 00:38:58.340
protecting all sentient beings. Then the Buddha says: Okay, but before you go there, please brush your teeth every day, okay?

00:38:59.620 --> 00:39:03.860


00:39:03.860 --> 00:39:06.160


00:39:06.168 --> 00:39:07.679


00:39:08.640 --> 00:39:10.800
You might think: those aren't really important precepts. But it's precisely these small things that create the Buddha's Pure Land. These are things Bodhisattvas often do—small things of kindness towards others. Of course, if everyone in the world could do that, they would stop a nuclear war or something similar; that's obvious. But are you a good enough person to

00:39:11.840 --> 00:39:17.340
even think about not letting others smell your breath, afraid of making them uncomfortable? If

00:39:17.360 --> 00:39:22.500
you are very sensitive to any small things that might hurt others, then

00:39:23.440 --> 00:39:25.840
we can say—you uphold your morality (precepts).

00:39:26.640 --> 00:39:34.820
So, it is these small details that ultimately adorn your Pure Land. You

00:39:34.920 --> 00:39:36.160
can see this in the next picture.

00:39:40.080 --> 00:39:44.640
This person is decorating a Christmas tree.

00:39:46.840 --> 00:39:48.760
I don't know if you've ever decorated a Christmas tree,

00:39:48.760 --> 00:39:50.880
but for those of us who grew up in Christian tradition, our

00:39:51.680 --> 00:39:53.680
parents would have us decorate Christmas trees.

00:39:54.400 --> 00:39:56.800
When putting on the last decoration,

00:39:57.440 --> 00:40:00.580
something cool happens.

00:40:01.260 --> 00:40:04.100
Everyone looks at the tree and says: "Done!"

00:40:04.100 --> 00:40:05.880
They say: "Yes, finished!"

00:40:06.400 --> 00:40:10.080
He says: "Wait a minute, we need to put one more over there."

00:40:10.720 --> 00:40:16.500
This Christmas tree (the last decoration) is a toothbrush.

00:40:16.500 --> 00:40:20.520
This is the final detail that leads to your Buddhahood.

00:40:20.880 --> 00:40:27.280
It is these small things that create Buddhahood,

00:40:27.280 --> 00:40:29.700
not those major events, not those big things. It is the

00:40:29.800 --> 00:40:37.560
attention to small details that make others happy that makes Buddha.

00:40:40.160 --> 00:40:42.160
Next,

00:40:44.160 --> 00:40:47.540
see if you remember this, here's a hint
—Yamantika.

00:40:55.680 --> 00:40:59.560
This is a famous story from the Stages of the Path to Enlightenment.

00:41:00.480 --> 00:41:04.720
Monks and nuns are supposed to confess twice a month,

00:41:05.440 --> 00:41:09.760
openly admitting the mistakes they have made.

00:41:11.600 --> 00:41:13.600
The teacher said, "

00:41:13.839 --> 00:41:16.959
They strike the gunty, they strike that gunty. It

00:41:17.839 --> 00:41:21.199
's a special piece of wood, it looks insignificant.

00:41:21.840 --> 00:41:26.200
Then you hit it with another small stick, making a thud, thud, thud sound.

00:41:26.640 --> 00:41:32.000
Before metal became widespread, this was an ancient bell.

00:41:32.000 --> 00:41:35.800
They would strike a wooden board.

00:41:36.080 --> 00:41:38.600
When you hear that sound, you have to make a confession.

00:41:38.600 --> 00:41:39.980
They still do that now."

00:41:40.240 --> 00:41:42.720
I made a gunty for my teacher, he wanted one.

00:41:43.840 --> 00:41:46.140
We made one according to the correct size. There

00:41:46.480 --> 00:41:48.180
are many rules for making it.

00:41:48.420 --> 00:41:50.420
When you hear the sound of the gunty,

00:41:50.880 --> 00:41:52.880
you should... put it here.

00:41:53.200 --> 00:41:55.980
You hold it like this, and then strike it like this.

00:41:56.560 --> 00:42:00.060
Then all the monks and nuns have to make confessions. The teacher said: "

00:42:00.800 --> 00:42:04.320
Hey, they've struck that gunty, let's go." The

00:42:05.119 --> 00:42:07.838
student said: "No, I'm not going to make a confession today." The teacher said: "

00:42:08.640 --> 00:42:10.640


00:42:11.040 --> 00:42:15.839


00:42:16.480 --> 00:42:17.780
What?" Making a confession is one of the main commitments of a monk.

00:42:17.780 --> 00:42:19.199


00:42:20.000 --> 00:42:22.740
The teacher asked: What are you saying? He said, "I don't need to go

00:42:22.800 --> 00:42:26.440
today." The teacher asked, "What do you mean by saying you don't need to go today?" The student said: "Have you forgotten that you gave me the Vajrabhairava empowerment yesterday?" I

00:42:26.960 --> 00:42:29.500
am Vajrabhairava,

00:42:29.500 --> 00:42:31.600
I have attained Buddhahood, I no longer need to go to confession ceremonies.

00:42:32.480 --> 00:42:34.820
The teacher then grabbed his ear and

00:42:34.820 --> 00:42:36.640
said: What are you? ! Are you Vajrabhairava?

00:42:36.920 --> 00:42:41.900
Vajrabhairava also needs to go to confession with me, right away!

00:42:43.200 --> 00:42:46.660
This means:
Don't tell me you're a great practitioner of Tantra, that

00:42:47.600 --> 00:42:52.540
you've transcended morality, and that you now have a higher perspective.

00:42:53.360 --> 00:42:56.480
That idea is completely wrong!

00:42:57.440 --> 00:43:00.720
If you receive a secret empowerment,

00:43:01.200 --> 00:43:04.180
then you should make confessions every morning, and so on.

00:43:04.380 --> 00:43:07.000
You should do this more often than others

00:43:07.000 --> 00:43:10.980
because it will empower your Tantric practice, which

00:43:11.180 --> 00:43:15.760
is being kind to others and being honest when you make mistakes. Next image:

00:43:16.080 --> 00:43:18.080


00:43:21.120 --> 00:43:23.440
This is a sad picture.

00:43:23.440 --> 00:43:28.760
We always think that morality is the foundation of our practice, the basis of our

00:43:29.100 --> 00:43:31.260
practice.

00:43:31.800 --> 00:43:34.480
However, Pabongka Rinpoche turned it around in a way.

00:43:35.680 --> 00:43:37.335
This picture is perfect.

00:43:37.340 --> 00:43:40.880
He said: Imagine an apple tree.

00:43:41.040 --> 00:43:44.640
Someone cut it in half. Actually, he used a palm tree as an example. Someone is

00:43:46.000 --> 00:43:50.980
cutting down the tree. They cut off the crown.

00:43:51.280 --> 00:43:53.760
Now you can't get leaves. Not a

00:43:53.980 --> 00:43:56.720
single leaf can grow.

00:43:56.960 --> 00:43:58.980
Therefore, you can't get flowers either.

00:44:00.000 --> 00:44:03.599
Therefore, you can't harvest the fruit that comes from the flowers.

00:44:04.400 --> 00:44:06.420
You will get nothing.

00:44:06.640 --> 00:44:12.160
If a person is not kind to others day after day, moment by moment,

00:44:13.360 --> 00:44:17.400
they cut off all the opportunities—the

00:44:18.640 --> 00:44:22.140
opportunities to harvest the beautiful fruit that comes from practice.

00:44:22.240 --> 00:44:23.840
Next image:

00:44:30.360 --> 00:44:33.840
This idea comes from something my teacher once asked me. I'm

00:44:35.820 --> 00:44:38.080
sorry, I asked my teacher.

00:44:38.080 --> 00:44:41.600
I don't know if you remember, but I asked him about the

00:44:42.720 --> 00:44:47.860
first of the five paths—the path of accumulation.

00:44:50.120 --> 00:44:54.060
When you personally encounter a calamity, you reach the first path.

00:44:54.380 --> 00:44:57.600
But in the Bodhisattva path, you only

00:44:58.000 --> 00:45:00.136
reach the first path when you attain Bodhicitta.

00:45:00.136 --> 00:45:04.239
So I ask: I don't understand what calamity is associated with Bodhicitta?

00:45:05.680 --> 00:45:11.280
He said: No, no, that theme (the path of accumulation in the Bodhisattva path) is still calamity. It's

00:45:11.520 --> 00:45:15.540
just that it's a calamity for all sentient beings.

00:45:15.540 --> 00:45:20.760
All sentient beings in the universe have the same calamity.

00:45:22.060 --> 00:45:28.520
That common calamity is the beginning of the five paths.

00:45:28.660 --> 00:45:34.080
For a Bodhisattva, contemplating that calamity is the beginning of the five paths.

00:45:34.200 --> 00:45:35.780
So really, it's all the same.

00:45:36.160 --> 00:45:40.320
This little dog is in pain, but now all the little dogs in the basket are in pain.

00:45:42.560 --> 00:45:44.560
We are all in the same boat.

00:45:44.720 --> 00:45:47.360
That is the beginning of Bodhicitta. Next

00:45:50.920 --> 00:45:52.140
picture: There's

00:45:52.143 --> 00:45:56.860
someone shaking hands with someone in an office.

00:45:57.440 --> 00:46:00.920
I imagine: the lady is introducing them.

00:46:00.920 --> 00:46:03.840
This is Joe, he works in the advertising department.

00:46:03.840 --> 00:46:07.360
This is Sam, he works in the computer department.

00:46:08.000 --> 00:46:10.000
They shake hands with each other. Do

00:46:10.720 --> 00:46:12.720
you remember what this theme is?

00:46:17.680 --> 00:46:21.260
This is a really fun exercise.

00:46:21.260 --> 00:46:23.119
We should close our eyes and

00:46:23.920 --> 00:46:26.639
think about the person we annoy the most, and

00:46:27.440 --> 00:46:29.960
see if we make ourselves feel annoyed. The

00:46:30.200 --> 00:46:32.500
problem with this kind of exercise is:

00:46:32.500 --> 00:46:34.900
after ten minutes, you forget it's just an exercise and

00:46:35.760 --> 00:46:37.760
you actually start to feel annoyed!

00:46:38.640 --> 00:46:40.640
Let me see if I can make myself upset.

00:46:41.200 --> 00:46:42.660
What do you do?

00:46:42.820 --> 00:46:44.640
I need to think about the person who caused me trouble this week.

00:46:44.640 --> 00:46:46.240
"Okay, let's begin."

00:46:47.040 --> 00:46:49.244
Then, slowly, this person starts to tremble.

00:46:49.244 --> 00:46:50.940
You ask, "What's wrong?"

00:46:51.080 --> 00:46:52.880
"I'm getting upset."

00:46:52.880 --> 00:46:54.720
The experiment is a success.

00:46:56.180 --> 00:46:59.140
If it were your teacher, they would say,

00:46:59.680 --> 00:47:03.680
"Check how you felt when you first started thinking about this person."

00:47:04.560 --> 00:47:07.199
What did that feel like? What are you feeling in your heart?

00:47:08.080 --> 00:47:11.560
I don't know how you will feel, but my heart feels a little uncomfortable. When

00:47:11.740 --> 00:47:16.500
I think about someone or a problem that bothers me,

00:47:17.200 --> 00:47:21.600
I start to feel a little uncomfortable here or there.

00:47:22.260 --> 00:47:28.160
I deliberately create tension in my body.

00:47:28.800 --> 00:47:32.560
He said: Let's do an exercise:

00:47:32.560 --> 00:47:35.460
Try to induce some tension in your mind.

00:47:35.920 --> 00:47:38.960
Then look at that tension and understand it,

00:47:38.960 --> 00:47:40.720
as if you are shaking hands with someone.

00:47:41.680 --> 00:47:45.180
Start to understand what that feels like.

00:47:45.680 --> 00:47:51.700
When the trouble, the negative emotion, first comes to your mind, continue

00:47:51.700 --> 00:47:52.880
this exercise.

00:47:53.840 --> 00:47:56.940
Once you feel better and forget about that person,

00:47:57.000 --> 00:47:58.120
think about them again and see if you feel upset again.

00:47:58.800 --> 00:48:00.400


00:48:00.420 --> 00:48:02.000
See if you become upset again.

00:48:02.560 --> 00:48:05.060
Try to familiarize yourself with this feeling and shake hands with it.

00:48:05.060 --> 00:48:07.780
"Hi, I'm Geshe Michael."

00:48:07.780 --> 00:48:09.320
"Hi, what's your name?"

00:48:09.580 --> 00:48:12.560
"I'm starting to feel upset about this person."

00:48:12.580 --> 00:48:15.680
"It's nice to meet you, now I know what you look like." "

00:48:16.240 --> 00:48:19.839
Now I can be wary of you, I can avoid you from now on." Next. This one is

00:48:20.400 --> 00:48:22.400


00:48:26.880 --> 00:48:29.440
called Visiting the Center of the Sun. The

00:48:31.520 --> 00:48:36.480
theme of this stage of the path is "Love in the Time of Pandemic." The

00:48:39.599 --> 00:48:42.959
virus is a big deal; it has spread all over the world. I've

00:48:43.680 --> 00:48:46.960
lived for a long time, and I thought I had seen everything.

00:48:47.760 --> 00:48:53.500
After I turned 60, I thought nothing new would happen anymore.

00:48:53.780 --> 00:48:56.000
I was prepared for anything that was going to happen.

00:48:56.940 --> 00:49:00.940
I'd seen it all, nothing could bother me anymore.

00:49:00.940 --> 00:49:04.560
Then this virus came, threatening everyone in the world.

00:49:05.200 --> 00:49:09.760
I thought: Wow, this is huge, it's all over the planet.

00:49:12.160 --> 00:49:15.700
I don't know if you've ever experienced this, but it happened to me.

00:49:15.920 --> 00:49:21.100
This might be the ninth unwholesome action, referring to morbid expectations. Taking pleasure in

00:49:22.080 --> 00:49:24.240
other people's misfortunes.

00:49:24.246 --> 00:49:29.640
When I heard that famous, particularly annoying person was sick, I certainly didn't wish them dead or

00:49:30.780 --> 00:49:35.760
anything, but...

00:49:36.480 --> 00:49:40.920
I would think: See, I said it—it's terrible to be a bad person. Then I

00:49:41.520 --> 00:49:44.560
caught myself thinking this. This feels

00:49:45.760 --> 00:49:47.800
huge. It seems like

00:49:48.100 --> 00:49:54.800
this problem has spread all over the planet. This feels overwhelming.

00:49:55.600 --> 00:50:00.540


00:50:01.120 --> 00:50:06.640
But after 10 years of studying the stages of the path, we've just entered... We've just entered the path of the superior being

00:50:06.720 --> 00:50:11.380
(the path of higher beings).

00:50:12.400 --> 00:50:18.640
We're about to begin learning the concept of Bodhicitta. What is Bodhicitta? It

00:50:18.640 --> 00:50:19.840


00:50:19.920 --> 00:50:21.633
doesn't refer to the consciousness of enlightenment.

00:50:21.633 --> 00:50:25.700
Forget that terrible translation, it's utterly awful. It refers to a wish

00:50:26.500 --> 00:50:33.120
—I want to become a Buddha so that I can help all beings. There is a direct experience of it, the same

00:50:34.319 --> 00:50:36.479


00:50:37.119 --> 00:50:40.180
way as directly experiencing emptiness.

00:50:40.180 --> 00:50:47.960
Those parallel experiences are what we must go through in this life. Again, it must happen in

00:50:48.500 --> 00:50:51.600
meditation.

00:50:52.560 --> 00:50:56.101
We have described something extraordinary...

00:50:56.101 --> 00:50:59.420
What do you call it? ...A breakthrough, an introductory experience. It happens when

00:51:01.020 --> 00:51:04.560


00:51:05.760 --> 00:51:10.300
you enter a deep meditative state

00:51:10.500 --> 00:51:14.100
because time and space both originate from seeds. If you can manage these seeds, you can compress time and space in less than

00:51:14.320 --> 00:51:16.320


00:51:16.720 --> 00:51:24.180
half an hour of meditation. You can truly visit every living being in the universe, including animals, insects, birds, and fish. In just half an hour, you can communicate one-on-one with each of them. You can make commitments to each of them. You meet them, and you see that they are all suffering, each going through a difficult time, constantly worrying about the future.

00:51:25.120 --> 00:51:29.740


00:51:30.300 --> 00:51:33.040


00:51:33.760 --> 00:51:40.460
You

00:51:40.800 --> 00:51:43.460
can go to each one individually and say, "I will handle this, relax." I started working when I was in college. I received a scholarship,

00:51:44.160 --> 00:51:48.820


00:51:48.840 --> 00:51:54.400


00:51:55.020 --> 00:51:56.960
but they said: You must work a certain number of hours each week. I later found out it was 30 hours a week. I had to drive a truck. Actually, they first took me to a coffee shop. They said:

00:51:57.600 --> 00:52:00.420
You have to mop the floor in the coffee

00:52:00.500 --> 00:52:03.140


00:52:03.920 --> 00:52:05.000


00:52:05.000 --> 00:52:07.040


00:52:07.680 --> 00:52:09.680


00:52:12.200 --> 00:52:13.860


00:52:14.960 --> 00:52:17.400


00:52:17.400 --> 00:52:19.840
shop. I gave up after less than 10 hours; I gave up on the first day. Then they said: You can drive a truck. I said: That sounds fun, I'll drive a truck.

00:52:19.920 --> 00:52:23.440
I drove a truck for 5 years. One of us was a permanent employee at the university named John Strong. His name was John Strong; he was

00:52:24.480 --> 00:52:26.328


00:52:26.328 --> 00:52:28.319
Polish, 7 feet tall, and very strong. Everyone was afraid of him when they saw him, very afraid of him, but he was a very good person. He would bring donuts to work. He was from Trenton, New Jersey. He would do the best things for us, and he would always protect us. One day

00:52:29.360 --> 00:52:32.120
we crashed a truck in two. We crashed the truck into a tree,

00:52:33.840 --> 00:52:36.160


00:52:36.480 --> 00:52:41.480


00:52:41.940 --> 00:52:47.880


00:52:49.360 --> 00:52:52.560


00:52:52.560 --> 00:52:54.620


00:52:55.520 --> 00:53:01.400


00:53:03.440 --> 00:53:06.920
and then the truck broke in two. He covered for us: "Oh, these screws weren't very tight. I don't know how, the truck just split open. Don't blame these guys. Don't blame these young people. They were just driving."

00:53:06.920 --> 00:53:09.060


00:53:09.680 --> 00:53:12.400
Then

00:53:13.040 --> 00:53:18.160
he winked at us and said, "I'll protect you.

00:53:18.160 --> 00:53:22.000
I'll protect all of you." When I contemplate Bodhicitta, I always think of him. You will directly see every

00:53:22.640 --> 00:53:24.640
sentient being in the universe.

00:53:25.040 --> 00:53:27.040


00:53:27.440 --> 00:53:28.575
Then you will

00:53:28.575 --> 00:53:31.600
say: "John will protect you. I will protect you. Don't worry. Don't worry, I'll protect you." This is Bodhicitta. You should have this experience.

00:53:33.000 --> 00:53:35.560


00:53:36.260 --> 00:53:40.680
You should strive to have this experience. You must meditate. You must learn Bodhicitta. You must learn the part about Bodhicitta in the Stages of the Path. You must do all these steps, such as exchanging self and others. One day you will have this experience. You will meet every sentient being.

00:53:41.200 --> 00:53:45.200
You would say to them: I'll take care of you, don't

00:53:45.839 --> 00:53:47.919
worry, I'll protect you. Mike will take care of you, or Tim, or Serge. Don't worry, don't be nervous, I'm good at this! That is the exact feeling of

00:53:48.960 --> 00:53:51.421


00:53:51.421 --> 00:53:54.240


00:53:54.880 --> 00:53:56.594


00:53:56.594 --> 00:53:58.880
Bodhicitta, a personal commitment. Why are we talking about this?

00:53:59.920 --> 00:54:02.000


00:54:03.099 --> 00:54:05.099


00:54:05.680 --> 00:54:09.780
You will do this in countless worlds. When you do this, and one day you can do it, you will do it in countless

00:54:10.400 --> 00:54:13.920


00:54:14.000 --> 00:54:18.559
worlds, making a commitment directly to every being in countless worlds. Such an act is effortless in eradicating a virus in one world. (This virus) is insignificant. A virus that endangers seven or eight billion people is

00:54:19.200 --> 00:54:21.200


00:54:21.600 --> 00:54:24.080


00:54:25.840 --> 00:54:28.720


00:54:29.920 --> 00:54:31.920


00:54:32.400 --> 00:54:34.146


00:54:34.146 --> 00:54:36.260


00:54:36.720 --> 00:54:39.120
nothing compared to Bodhicitta. It's like if you spill ketchup on a shirt and then send that shirt into the center of the sun, where it's 25 million degrees Fahrenheit, the ketchup stain will likely disappear. You won't have to worry about the ketchup stain anymore. Work hard for your Bodhicitta. You will

00:54:40.640 --> 00:54:46.960


00:54:48.000 --> 00:54:51.392
destroy the virus,

